  "id": "ironsidegym",
  "note": "IRONSIDE GYM: a boxing and weights gym on the corner of Ironside Street and Lever Lane.\n\nThe tile's prose: a two-storey brick works with the ground floor knocked through into one long\nroom and every window along it propped open on a stick, because the room needs the air. Benches,\nracks of odd plates, and a ring with its ropes taped. IRONSIDE GYM painted across the brick over\nthe door in letters a yard high.\n\nSo it is a plain brick block with steel-framed windows: four tall ones along the ground floor, lit\nwarm, and the door between them under a small hood. The name is painted straight onto the brick\nabove the ground floor (`bare`), once. The corner blade says `$trade`, which resolves to GYM.\nThe upper floor is a row of smaller steel windows. One flank carries the fire escape, the back has\na roller door for deliveries, and the roof has a tank and a vent stack.\n\nIt replaced Tine & Temper, a kitchenware shop on this tile, in October 2026.",
  "pal": "ty_unit_brick",
